1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,011
Every day, sunlight delivers more energy to Earth than we use in a year.

2
00:00:04,011 --> 00:00:09,499
Solar panels capture that light and photovoltaic cells convert it into direct current electricity.

3
00:00:09,499 --> 00:00:13,770
An inverter changes the current into power that household appliances can use.

4
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:17,861
A family can generate clean electricity on the roof of an ordinary home.

5
00:00:17,861 --> 00:00:22,244
When the sun sets, a home battery stores extra daytime power for evening demand.

6
00:00:22,244 --> 00:00:25,887
Connected homes can send surplus electricity back to the local grid.

7
00:00:25,887 --> 00:00:31,461
At utility scale, broad solar farms turn open land into productive clean energy fields.

8
00:00:31,461 --> 00:00:36,693
Wind turbines and healthy landscapes complement solar power and help lower carbon emissions.

9
00:00:36,693 --> 00:00:41,794
With thoughtful planning, renewable energy makes communities more resilient and the future brighter.

